## Task 3: Document, verify, and benchmark parallel cache refresh

Context: Document and validate the parallel Lakehouse companion rebuild
introduced in Task 2 (commit e5e6ced7). Run the mandatory test suite, run IDE
diagnostics on the modified files, and measure actual wall-time improvement on
the BIGCustomers Lakehouse domain against the prior serial baseline of 128.62
seconds.

Changes:

1. docs/optimizations.md
   Expand the companion-snapshot paragraph (§1) to state that rebuilds are
   full snapshots (not incremental), that Lakehouse rebuilds four or five
   companions concurrently via `ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=min(5, N))` where
   N is the scheduled companion count (five when `entity_search_asserted`
   resolves, four otherwise), that each worker uses the stateless per-request
   SQL client so the CTAS statements run in true parallel, and that per-companion
   and total timings are logged at INFO. Document that Lakebase runs DDL
   outside a transaction, replaces all companion data in a single Postgres
   transaction, and runs ANALYZE in a separate non-transactional step.
   Add new §18 "Parallel companion rebuild — measured performance" with the
   before/after benchmark table, per-companion timing breakdown, and smoke-check
   confirmation.

Modified files:
- docs/optimizations.md
- changelogs/v0.9.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-09-17.log

Diagnostics: no new linter errors on DeltaFlatStore.py or
test_delta_flat_store.py.

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" → 6190 passed, 304 skipped,
