## Document strict No-LLM behavior

Context: Complete the No-LLM AI gating work by documenting that an empty saved
domain target is a strict opt-out. LLM actions stay visible but unavailable
until a model is selected and saved in Domain Information → AI, while
deterministic reasoning and validation remain available.

Changes:

1. Backend domain guard and routes
   Reject every scoped Ontology, Mapping, Graph Chat, and Analytics LLM request
   before task creation or model invocation, use the saved target as authority,
   and remove Graph LLM auto-discovery.
2. Global frontend availability gate
   Start fail-closed, follow saved domain state, block mouse and keyboard
   activation with common guidance, and preserve independent permission,
   lifecycle, ARIA, and native-disabled state.
3. Domain-scoped LLM controls
   Mark Ontology generation, Assistant, automatic icons, AI Business Rules,
   Mapping Auto-Map/SQL, Graph Chat, and Analytics Interpret while leaving the
   AI tab, Browse picker, and deterministic actions usable.
4. README.md and docs/user-guide.md
   Document the strict opt-out, visible unavailable actions, re-enable path,
   live availability refresh, and deterministic reasoning and validation.
5. Tests
   Cover the backend guard and route contract, saved-target precedence,
   fail-closed UI behavior, complete trigger inventory, and picker exclusions.

