## Synchronize the LLM gate after domain save

Context: Saving No LLM or restoring a model in Domain Information left the
global LLM availability gate stale until the asynchronous navbar refresh
completed. The Information form's actual Save path auto-saved through the
navbar flow without parsing its response, so an LLM-dependent action could
still issue a request after No LLM had been persisted.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/domain/js/domain.js
   Apply the saved response's LLM endpoint to the existing global availability
   gate synchronously on successful fallback saves.
2. src/front/static/global/js/navbar.js
   Parse and validate the actual pre-registry auto-save response, then update
   the gate from authoritative saved data before cache invalidation.
3. tests/units/front/test_no_llm_save_gate_sync.py
   Execute both real save handlers under Node and cover empty, whitespace,
   configured, ordering, HTTP failure, and application failure behavior.

